---
title: Biome
description: First-class Biome and Ultracite integration.
---

Biome formats and lints. Canonicalize rewrites Tailwind semantics. Run both.

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && biome check --write .",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && biome ci ."
  }
}
```

With Ultracite:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && ultracite fix",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && ultracite check"
  }
}
```

Recommended order: **canonicalize first**, then Biome, so format runs on canonical classes.

/docs/integrations/eslint.mdx:
---
title: ESLint
description: Compose with ESLint and eslint-plugin-tailwindcss.
---

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "fix": "tailwind-canonicalize . --write --safe && eslint . --fix",
    "check": "tailwind-canonicalize . --check && eslint ."
  }
}
```

Use `eslint-plugin-tailwindcss` for **class order / invalid names** if you want — not for arbitrary→scale rewrites. That is this tool’s job.

lint-staged:

```json
{
  "*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}": [
    "tailwind-canonicalize --write",
    "eslint --fix --max-warnings=0"
  ]
}
```

